 "text": "Hello there! How are you today? Weddings are about enjoying the variety, not making everyone match. Would you mind if each one wore the same basic underlayers? Sure thing. Not at all, they're the very worst thing to buy for someone else. Okay on the bridesmaid dresses. A quick call to each of them to see what they already have, and then a decision based on what they have and what's available. Then stick simple solid colors. If one wears black, a white or neutral skin tone as base and add a color or two with earrings and necklace gives the cleanest look.",
